   Subcommands
@X03
          @X0BS           selects ALL conferences
          @X0B#           selects a specific conference
          @X0B#-#         selects a range of conferences
@X0F
   Description
@X03
      While modifying a user record the last question asked is
      "Select Conferences" which brings up a conference registration
      screen if you answer in the affirmative.

      After selecting the conference(s) to act upon the system will
      ask you for the flags you wish to use for that conference.  The
      possible answers are as follows:

@X0B      Registration Flags@X03
      ------------------

           @X0B R @X03            = Caller is registered in conference if his
                            subscription has not expired.

           @X0B X @X03            = Caller is registered in conference even
                            if his subscription has expired.

           @X0B L @X03            = Caller is locked out of the conference.

           @X0B S @X03            = Caller has chosen to scan this conference.

           @X0B C @X03            = Caller is made a "sysop" temporarily while
                            in this conference.

      Note that if a conference is flagged as PUBLIC and the caller
      has sufficient security to join the conference he may do so
      regardless of the "R" and "X" flags unless his "L" flag is
      turned on to indicate that he is locked out of that conference.
@X0F
   Examples
@X03
      To register a user in a conference and mark the conference for scanning
      enter the following:
@X0E
          RS
@X03
      To register the user in a conference even if they are expired enter the
      following:
@X0E
          RX
